#====================================================================
# DRAFT-socket-wrapper-musl-lfs64-mmsg-ohos.kv
# socket_wrapper 1.5.2 musl LFS64 宏冲突 + mmsg 原型不匹配 + HarmonyOS 平台 soname 丢失
# Draft only. Do not promote into knowledge/graph until promoted.
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-socket-wrapper-musl-lfs64-mmsg-ohos
trigger_tool:           clang|cmake|conan
phase:                  building|configuring|packaging
error_signature:        redefinition of 'fopen'|redefinition of 'open'|redefinition of 'openat'|
                         conflicting types for 'recvmmsg'|conflicting types for 'sendmmsg'|
                         previous declaration is here.*sys/socket.h|缺少 DT_SONAME
severity:               3
category:               toolchain|musl|libc|portability|cmake|ohos
match_keywords:         musl, OHOS, LFS64, fopen64, open64, openat64, recvmmsg, sendmmsg,
                         unsigned int flags, conflicting types, redefinition, _GNU_SOURCE,
                         check_prototype_definition, DT_SONAME, soname, HarmonyOS,
                         CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME, versioned shared library
title:                  LD_PRELOAD interposition libraries on musl/OHOS hit LFS64 macro redefinitions, mmsg prototype mismatches, and lose DT_SONAME when cmake sees the host as HarmonyOS
root_cause:             Three independent musl/OHOS differences break glibc-oriented
                         interposition code:
                         (1) musl maps fopen64/open64/openat64 to plain fopen/open/openat
                         via macros when _GNU_SOURCE is defined, so `FILE *fopen64(...)`
                         definitions expand into redefinitions of fopen.
                         (2) musl declares `int recvmmsg(int, struct mmsghdr *, unsigned
                         int, unsigned int, struct timespec *)` and `int sendmmsg(int,
                         struct mmsghdr *, unsigned int, unsigned int)` — flags are
                         unsigned int — while upstream only knows the glibc (int flags)
                         and FreeBSD (ssize_t) prototypes.
                         (3) When the OHOS-adapted Conan toolchain leaves CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME
                         as the host-detected "HarmonyOS", cmake 4.x treats it as an
                         unknown platform, CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_SONAME_FLAG stays empty,
                         and versioned shared libraries are linked without -Wl,-soname,
                         so packaged .so files lose DT_SONAME (L5a quality gate).
affected_scope:         Any LD_PRELOAD/interposition or socket-oriented C library that
                         defines LFS64 entry points, exports recvmmsg/sendmmsg, or ships
                         versioned .so files and is built on the OHOS PC device with the
                         ohos-aarch64 Conan profile (cwrap family: socket_wrapper,
                         uid_wrapper, nss_wrapper, pam_wrapper, and similar).
verification_cmd:       /data/service/hnp/bin/llvm-readelf -d <pkg>/lib/lib<name>.so | grep SONAME; nm -D <pkg>/lib/lib<name>.so | grep -E "fopen64|recvmmsg"

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           undef-lfs64-macros + prototype-detection + explicit-system-name
rec_description:        (1) Add `#undef fopen64/open64/openat64` (guarded by __OHOS__)
                         immediately before each interposed LFS64 definition.
                         (2) Add check_prototype_definition probes for the musl
                         prototypes (HAVE_RECVMMSG_UNSIGNED_FLAGS /
                         HAVE_SENDMMSG_UNSIGNED_FLAGS), declare them in config.h.cmake,
                         and extend every signature chain (typedef, libc_ wrapper,
                         swrap_ implementation, exported symbol) with the musl branch.
                         (3) In the Conan recipe generate(), set
                         tc.cache_variables["CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME"]="OHOS" and
                         CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR="aarch64" so cmake restores the
                         -Wl,-soname link flag and the versioned .so.0 layout.
rec_verified_on:        socket-wrapper/1.5.2 aarch64 OHOS 6.0, clang 15.0.4, cmake 4.1.2
rec_evidence:           conan create 100% upstream tests (29/29 registered), test_package
                         LD_PRELOAD loopback redirection passed, readelf shows
                         SONAME [libsocket_wrapper.so.0]; archives/s/socket-wrapper/1.5.2/
                         reports/w3-local-ci.log L5_RESULT=pass
last_updated:           2026-09-02
author:                 socket-wrapper adaptation task (feat/socket-wrapper-1.5.2)
